Derived files, and how they were changed (License section 4(b)):

  - agents/*.md
      The persona structure and the "Core Mandates" section (read-only,
      fresh context, no chitchat) are adapted from the EGM persona files
      (agents/*.md). Changed: rewritten for tabletop RPG campaign review and
      brainstorming; roles, checks, and output formats are new.
  - .claude-plugin/agents/*.md
      Follow the EGM Claude Code adapter format (.claude-plugin/agents/*.md):
      read-only tools, omitClaudeMd, and a pointer to the canonical persona.
      Changed: point at this plugin's personas.
  - plugin.json, .claude-plugin/plugin.json, .claude-plugin/marketplace.json
      Follow the EGM manifest layout. Changed: this plugin's identity and
      agent list.
  - skills/campaign-brainstorm/SKILL.md
      The workflow shape (clarify, readiness gate, parallel Goldfish lenses,
      brief, handoff), the Delegation section, and several constraints are
      adapted from EGM skills/egm-brainstorm/SKILL.md. Changed: rewritten for
      campaign prep; the eight-step questions, seven lenses, and post-session
      debrief are new.
  - skills/campaign-draft/SKILL.md, skills/campaign-review/SKILL.md
      Follow the section-by-section approval gates of EGM egm-draft and the
      fresh-reviewer passes and Delegation section of EGM egm-review.
      Changed: rewritten for campaign documents; sections, passes, and report
      format are new.

All other files (the standard, templates, tests, and documentation) are
original to this plugin. No EGM files are included unchanged.

An earlier version of this plugin (dsh-egm-campaign) targeted dsh-egm
(https://github.com/dryw/dsh-egm, by dryw, Apache License 2.0). No dsh-egm
code remains in this version, except as noted below.

  - docs/assets/protocol.d2
      The D2 diagram classes (participant, frame, loop, note, and line
      styles), the colour roles, and the sequence-diagram layout follow
      dsh-egm docs/assets/protocol.d2. Changed: participants, phases, and
      messages are new and describe campaign prep.
  - docs/assets/render.mjs
      Follows the approach of dsh-egm adapters/dsh/render_diagrams.mjs
      (title, ARIA label, and an adaptive canvas added after D2 renders).
      Changed: rewritten as a single-diagram script.

